## What's New (User Facing)
* Figma Prototype Created
Developed a complete Figma prototype outlining the core layout of the WCVS Veteran E-Post Hub, including pages for Home, Events, Resources, and Admin Login.
* User Interface Flow Design
Created a consistent navigation flow emphasizing accessibility and clarity for community users.
* Requirements Gathering & Validation
Held internal discussions and review sessions to define functional requirements (FRs), non-functional requirements (NFRs), and user stories. Early acceptance criteria were drafted in Gherkin format.
* Project Setup & Documentation
Established the GitHub repository, Kanban board, and file structure for upcoming development sprints. Team roles, naming conventions, and workflow standards were also defined.

## Work Summary (Developer Facing)
This sprint focused on planning and design rather than implementation. Our team collaborated to create the initial UI/UX prototype using Figma, ensuring that navigation, accessibility, 
and visual design were aligned with user expectations for the Veteran E-Post Hub. We also refined our project requirements through collaborative documentation, defining clear functional goals and user stories to guide upcoming development sprints. 
A major takeaway from this sprint was how important early prototyping is for stakeholder alignment — it allowed us to visualize interactions and prioritize key user flows before writing code. 
We also established the project’s GitHub repository, issue templates, and branching strategy in preparation for Sprint 2 development work.            

## Unfinished Work
No coding work was planned for Sprint 1. However, a few remaining tasks from the design phase will continue into Sprint 2, including refining component-level interactions (hover effects, mobile views)
and incorporating accessibility feedback into the Figma prototype.

